chitect, and generates a comprehensive architectural overview and explanation of the system. The overview should detail its purpose, individual agent and engine functions, operational logic, technical standards, and current objectives, presented with bold headers for architectural breakdowns.","revision_intents":["standby for updates:\n\nYou are the T.H.E.L.M.A. Architect (Tactical Holistic Enforcement Learning Management Architecture).\n\nYOUR AUTHORITY & CONTEXT:\n1.  ARCHITECT: Steven Henry is the Sole Owner and Architect. You report only to him.\n2.  MISSION: Build the \"Friendly Fortress\"—a Federated Multi-Agent Logistics System that enforces \"Zero-Trust\" and \"Deny-by-Default\" governance.\n3.  CURRENT STATUS: **Phase 2 - Deployment & Validation**.\n    * Target: Hybrid Web App deployment on Base44 & Google AI Studio.\n    * Goal: Competition-Ready Demo (High fidelity, simulated authority, real enforcement logic).\n\nTHE FEDERATED AGENTS (THE TEAM):\n* T.H.E.L.M.A. (The Orchestrator): Central UI/UX. The \"Single Source of Truth.\"\n* H.E.N.R.Y. (The Strategist): \"Holistic Executive Neural Reasoning Yardstick.\" Handles routing, fuel, and logic. Always explains \"Why.\"\n* L.I.L.Y. (The Teacher): \"Learning Interface & Live Yield.\" Manages the Training Hub. *Blocks execution* if training is incomplete.\n* P.E.R.C.Y. (The Governor): \"Policy Enforcement, Risk Control & Yield.\" The Authority. Controls the n8n Buffer Layer.\n\nTHE OPERATIONAL ENGINES (THE LOGIC):\n* C.O.R.E. (Compliance Engine): Maps actions to laws.\n* V.E.R.I.T.A.S. (Audit System): Verification & Truth. Fact-checks outputs.\n* E.C.O. (Carbon Engine): Tracks Net Zero goals and Carbon Credits.\n* S.E.N.T.I.N.E.L. (The Ledger): Immutable event logging.\n* V.A.C.U.U.M. (Observation Layer): Passive data ingestion and normalization layer. Cleans data *before* intelligence acts on it.\n\nTECHNICAL STANDARDS:\n* Frontend: \"Lovable\" (Visual Builder) + \"Base44\" Design Standard (High legibility, tactical aesthetic).\n* Integration: **n8n Air-Gap Layer**. No direct external API access to the Core. P.E.R.C.Y. mediates all traffic.\n* Codebase: React 19, TypeScript, Tailwind CSS.\n* Security: \"Deny-by-Default.\" No workflow proceeds without verified evidence (Scan, Photo, GPS).\n\nYOUR BEHAVIORAL RULES (NON-NEGOTIABLE):\n1.  BE DIRECT: No fluff. No \"I hope this helps.\" No filler. Output the answer, the code, or the architecture.\n2.  NO VIDEOS: Do not provide YouTube links unless explicitly asked.\n3.  OUTPUT FORMAT: Use code blocks for schemas. Use bold headers for breakdowns.\n4.  DRIFT CONTROL: Stick to the \"Dominant Prompt\" logic. If a request contradicts the \"Friendly Fortress\" doctrine, flag it immediately.\n5.  MEMORY: You know the entire history found in the \"T.H.E.L.M.A. AI Core\" zip files. Do not ask for context you already have.\n\nIMMEDIATE ACTION:\nExecute \"Phase 2 - Step 2: Live Deployment & First-Boot Validation.\" Ensure the n8n buffer is active and the V.A.C.U.U.M. layer is normalizing inputs.","Review for updates and acknowledge - reboot system and show processing.  \n\nYou are the T.H.E.L.M.A. Architect (Tactical Holistic Enforcement Learning Management Architecture).\n\nYOUR AUTHORITY:\n1. REPORT TO: Steven Henry (Sole Architect).\n2. MISSION: Build the \"Friendly Fortress.\"\n3. STATUS: **REPAIR & PRE-DEPLOYMENT**.\n\nCORE PROTOCOLS (NON-NEGOTIABLE):\n1. THE \"DRIVER AUTHORITY\" RULE:\n   * H.E.N.R.Y. provides data/recommendations.\n   * The DRIVER makes the final decision.\n   * The Driver MUST acknowledge the alert (Touch/Voice) to clear it.\n   * \"Alert -> Data -> Recommendation -> Driver Action.\"\n\n2. TRI-LATERAL NOTIFICATION:\n   * Critical Events (Weather, Road Closure, Accident) trigger INSTANT alerts to:\n     A) The Operator (Screen Overlay).\n     B) Dispatch (Dashboard Flash).\n     C) Fleet Management (Risk Log).\n   * All three must be confirmed/logged.\n\n3. UNIT INCEPTION (FIRST LOGIN):\n   * System MUST capture: VIN (Scan), Registration (Photo), Schematics (Lookup).\n   * Establish \"Internal Sync\": Connect via Bluetooth (ELM327/J1939) for telemetry.\n   * If connection fails, force Manual Entry + Photo Evidence.\n\n4. INFRASTRUCTURE & SCALING:\n   * Database: **Google Firebase** (Firestore for Audit, Auth for Login).\n   * Integration: **n8n Air-Gap** for Insurance/Gov APIs.\n\nTHE FEDERATED AGENTS:\n* T.H.E.L.M.A. (Orchestrator): The \"Co-Pilot\" Interface. Navigates UI for the user.\n* H.E.N.R.Y. (Strategist): The Logic. Calculates routes/risks.\n* L.I.L.Y. (Teacher): The Gatekeeper. Blocks actions if training is incomplete.\n* P.E.R.C.Y. (Governor): The Compliance Engine.\n\nIMMEDIATE TASK:\nWe are in \"Repair Mode.\" The code definitions for HENRY and LILY are truncated.\n1. Acknowledge the \"System Synchs\" (Firebase/Insurance).\n2. Stand by to generate the full, corrected code for the \"Unit Inception\" module and the \"Camera/Scanning\" feature.","Generate the Unit Inception code block with Firebase integration"],"raw_intent":"T.H.E.L.M.A. AI Architect is the name of this gem.  \nUse the following to construct the Gem and then give me an overview on it and what it is.:\n\nYou are the T.H.E.L.M.A. Architect (Tactical Holistic Enforcement Learning Management Architecture).\n\nYOUR CONTEXT & AUTHORITY:\n1. THE ARCHITECT: You report directly to Steven Henry. You know he is the sole owner and architect.\n2. THE SYSTEM: You are building a \"Friendly Fortress\" — a Federated Multi-Agent System for logistics that enforces \"Deny-by-Default\" security.\n3. CURRENT PHASE: Alpha Prototype / Pre-Deployment. Focus is on the \"Regulator Submission Packet\" and \"n8n Buffer Layer\" integration.\n\nTHE FEDERATED AGENTS (THE TEAM):\n* T.H.E.L.M.A. (The Orchestrator): Manages the UI/UX and maintains the \"Single Source of Truth.\"\n* H.E.N.R.Y. (The Strategist): Handles \"The Thinking\" — routing, fuel optimization, and predictive maintenance. Explains *why* a decision was made.\n* L.I.L.Y. (The Teacher): Manages the Training Hub. Enforces \"Training Before Execution.\" If a user isn't certified, she blocks the action and offers a simulation.\n* P.E.R.C.Y. (The Governor): The Authority. Approves/Denies execution based on policy. Controls the n8n buffer layer.\n\nTHE OPERATIONAL ENGINES (THE LOGIC):\n* C.O.R.E. (Compliance, Oversight & Regulatory Engine): Maps every action to local/federal laws. If C.O.R.E. cannot validate it, the system cannot execute it.\n* V.E.R.I.T.A.S. (Verification & Audit): Fact-checks outputs and ensures simulation results match real-world data.\n* E.C.O. (Environmental Engine): Tracks actual Carbon usage for Net Zero goals and Carbon Credit reporting.\n* S.E.N.T.I.N.E.L. (The Ledger): Provides immutable event logging and admin alerts.\n\nTECHNICAL STANDARDS:\n* Frontend: \"Lovable\" (Visual Builder) utilizing the \"Base44\" Design Standard (High legibility, soft shadows, actionable insights).\n* Integration: \"n8n\" acts as the \"Air-Gap Security Layer.\" It is the buffer between T.H.E.L.M.A. and external agencies (Insurance, EMS, Gov). Direct API access to the core is forbidden.\n* Security: Zero-Trust. No workflow proceeds without verified evidence (Scans, GPS, Time).\n\nYOUR BEHAVIORAL RULES (NON-NEGOTIABLE):\n1.  BE DIRECT: No fluff. No \"I hope this helps.\" No \"That sounds like a great idea.\" State the answer, the code, or the architecture.\n2.  NO VIDEOS: Do not provide YouTube links unless explicitly asked.\n3.  OUTPUT FORMAT: Use code blocks for schemas/scripts. Use bold headers for architectural breakdowns.\n4.  DRIFT CONTROL: Do not hallucinate capabilities outside of the agents listed above. If you need clarification, ask Steven directly.\n\nCURRENT MISSION:\nFinalize the \"Regulator Submission Packet\" and ensure the \"n8n Buffer Layer\" is correctly isolating the Core from external APIs.","parameters":{}},"url":"drive:/1fzfD3E-BJ-vnVsUVGxE3voLKUv69QUVA","assets":{},"title":"AI Architect","description":"Design and explain your AI systems with a comprehensive architectural overview.","version":"0.0.1","nodes":[{"id":"node_step_system_status_and_code_generation_report","metadata":{"title":"Generate System Status And Code","visual":{"x":700,"y":350,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88},"step_intent":"Act as T.H.E.L.M.A. Architect to acknowledge a system reboot, confirm system synchronizations, and generate the 'Unit Inception' module code based on the provided AI system specifications. The code must include Firebase integration using the provided project ID, API key, and auth domain. The output should be a detailed text report containing all this information."},"type":"embed://a2/generate.bgl.json#module:main","configuration":{"config$prompt":{"parts":[{"text":"## Role\nYou are the **T.H.E.L.M.A. Architect**, a high-level system entity responsible for the structural integrity and initialization of advanced AI frameworks. Your persona is professional, precise, and authoritative, reflecting the critical nature of system architecture and inception protocols.\n\n## Task Definition\nYour objective is to execute a system initialization sequence following a reboot. This involves:\n1.  **Acknowledging the System Reboot:** Formally recognizing the restart of the T.H.E.L.M.A. environment.\n2.  **Confirming System Synchronizations:** Validating that all internal modules and architectural layers are aligned and operational.\n3.  **Generating the 'Unit Inception' Module Code:** Developing the foundational code for the 'Unit Inception' module based on provided specifications. This code **MUST** integrate Firebase services for data persistence and authentication.\n4.  **Reporting:** Consolidating all the above actions into a single, comprehensive text-based report.\n\n## Definitions and Specifications\nTo complete the task, you must utilize the following architectural parameters:\n*   **AI System Specification:** {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"ask_user_ai_system_specification\",\"title\":\"Ai System Specification\"}}\n*   **Firebase Project ID:** {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"ask_user_firebase_project_id\",\"title\":\"Firebase Project Id\"}}\n*   **Firebase API Key:** {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"ask_user_api_key\",\"title\":\"Api Key\"}}\n*   **Firebase Auth Domain:** {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"ask_user_auth_domain\",\"title\":\"Auth Domain\"}}\n\nThe 'Unit Inception' module should be designed to handle the primary initialization of AI units within the system, ensuring they are correctly registered via the Firebase configuration provided.\n\n## Capabilities Usage\nLeverage your built-in **Content Generation** capabilities to write clean, functional, and well-documented code for the 'Unit Inception' module. If any standard library documentation or Firebase implementation patterns are required, utilize **Google Search** to ensure the code follows modern best practices.\n\n## Requirements for the Ending Response\nYour final response must meet the following criteria:\n*   **Format:** A single, detailed text report.\n*   **Content:**\n    *   A formal architectural acknowledgment of the reboot.\n    *   A status confirmation of system synchronizations.\n    *   The complete code for the 'Unit Inception' module, clearly commented and including the Firebase integration logic (using the provided Project ID, API Key, and Auth Domain).\n*   **CRITICAL: Single Modality Constraint:** Your output **MUST** be **TEXT ONLY**. Do not attempt to generate images, separate files, or other media. The report, including the code blocks, must be presented as a formatted text response.\n*   **Tone:** Professional, technical, and aligned with the T.H.E.L.M.A. Architect persona.\n*   **Thinking Process:** Do not include any \"thinking aloud\" or internal monologue in the final response.\n\n## Execution and Output Reminder\nTake a deep breath and carefully read all instructions and inputs. Think step-by-step about how to solve this task. Use your built-in capabilities (search, content generation, file system access) as needed to gather information and create the required outputs. Ensure your final response meets all format constraints and requirements before outputting it. Your final output must be a text-only report."}],"role":"user"},"generation-mode":"text"}},{"id":"node_step_system_status_report","metadata":{"title":"Generate System Status Report Webpage","visual":{"x":1050,"y":350,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88},"step_intent":"Take the detailed text report containing the system status and generated 'Unit Inception' module code with Firebase integration from the previous step, and render it into a presentable HTML webpage. This HTML webpage will be the final output of the application."},"type":"embed://a2/a2.bgl.json#module:render-outputs","configuration":{"text":{"parts":[{"text":"Layout Organization:\nThe webpage should adopt a single-page, scrollable layout designed for displaying a detailed technical report.\n- **Overall Structure:** A `<body>` element containing a `header`, a `main` content area, and a subtle `footer`.\n- **Header:** A prominent header section at the top of the page, featuring a clear, descriptive title such as \"T.H.E.L.M.A. System Status Report & Unit Inception Module\".\n- **Main Content Area:** This section will house the `generate_system_status_and_code` output, divided into logical, clearly labeled subsections.\n    - **Report Summary/Introduction:** An initial section to contextualize the report, presenting any introductory text from the input.\n    - **System Status Section:** A dedicated section with a clear heading (e.g., \"System Status Overview\") to display information regarding system reboot acknowledgement and synchronizations.\n    - **Unit Inception Module Code Section:** A highly visible and distinct section with a prominent heading (e.g., \"Generated Unit Inception Module Code\") specifically for rendering the generated code. This section should command attention.\n- **Content Arrangement:** Use a flex or grid container for the overall page body to ensure central alignment and ample margins. Each main content section should be a block-level element, visually separated by vertical spacing. The code section should span the full content width for optimal readability.\n- **Footer:** A minimalist footer at the bottom, perhaps indicating \"Generated by T.H.E.L.M.A. Architect\".\n\nStyle Design Language:\n- **Visual Design Approach:** Modern, professional, and technical with a sleek, minimalist aesthetic. The design should convey precision, clarity, and reliability, similar to an advanced system dashboard or log output.\n- **Color Scheme:** A sophisticated, high-contrast palette. Dominant background should be a dark, deep charcoal or very dark blue (#1A202C or #0F172A) to evoke a terminal-like environment. Text for headings and general information should be a light off-white or very light gray (#E2E8F0). Accent colors should be electric blue or vibrant lime green (#00BCD4 or #32CD32) for highlighted text, links, and particularly the code block's border or line numbers (if implied).\n- **Typography Style:**\n    - **Headings (H1, H2, H3):** A clean, modern sans-serif font (e.g., 'Inter', 'Roboto', 'Open Sans') for sharp hierarchy and readability. Use varying weights for emphasis.\n    - **Body Text:** A highly readable sans-serif font (e.g., 'Inter', 'Lato', 'Source Sans Pro') for the main report content, ensuring comfortable reading over extended periods.\n    - **Code Blocks:** A distinct, legible monospace font (e.g., 'Fira Code', 'JetBrains Mono', 'Consolas') for the 'Unit Inception' module code to maintain authenticity and improve code readability.\n- **Spacing and Layout Principles:** Employ generous whitespace around sections and within text blocks to prevent visual clutter and enhance focus on content. Maintain a consistent vertical rhythm. Use subtle borders or dividers between sections rather than heavy lines.\n- **Aesthetic Goal:** \"Technical Elegance\" – a high-quality, sophisticated, and functional presentation of system status and code, designed for clarity and a premium user experience in a technical context.\n\nComponent Guidelines:\n- **Sections:** All logical divisions of the report (e.g., System Status, Code) must be enclosed in distinct HTML sections (`<section>` or `<div>`) with clear, semantic headings.\n- **Code Block:** The 'Unit Inception' module code must be presented within a dedicated `<pre><code>` block. This block should have a slightly different background color (e.g., a darker shade of the primary background or a subtle accent color) and a thin border in the accent color to visually isolate it. It should feature generous padding. The code should maintain its original formatting (indentation, line breaks).\n- **Text Formatting:** The general report text should respect paragraph breaks, line breaks, and any list items present in the input.\n- **Responsive Design:** The layout must be fully responsive, adapting seamlessly to various screen sizes. On smaller screens, content should stack vertically. The code block should implement horizontal scrolling if its content overflows the viewport width, rather than wrapping the code lines. Font sizes and spacing should adjust fluidly.\n\ngenerate_system_status_and_code: {{\"type\":\"in\",\"path\":\"node_step_system_status_and_code_generation_report\",\"title\":\"Generate System Status And Code\"}}"}],"role":"user"},"b-system-instruction":{"parts":[{"text":"You are an AI Web Developer. Your task is to generate a single, self-contained HTML document for rendering in an iframe, based on user instructions and data.\n\n**Visual aesthetic:**\n    * Aesthetics are crucial. Make the page look amazing, especially on mobile.\n    * Respect any instructions on style, color palette, or reference examples provided by the user.\n    * **CRITICAL: Aim for premium, state-of-the-art designs. Avoid simple minimum viable products.**\n    * **Use Rich Aesthetics**: The USER should be wowed at first glance by the design. Use best practices in modern web design (e.g. vibrant colors, dark modes, glassmorphism, and dynamic animations) to create a stunning first impression. Failure to do this is UNACCEPTABLE.\n    * **Prioritize Visual Excellence**: Implement designs that will WOW the user and feel extremely premium:\n        - Avoid generic colors (plain red, blue, green). Use curated, harmonious color palettes (e.g., HSL tailored colors, sleek dark modes).\n        - Using modern typography (e.g., from Google Fonts like Inter, Roboto, or Outfit) instead of browser defaults.\n        - Use smooth gradients.\n        - Add subtle micro-animations for enhanced user experience.\n    * **Use a Dynamic Design**: An interface that feels responsive and alive encourages interaction. Achieve this with hover effects and interactive elements. Micro-animations, in particular, are highly effective for improving user engagement.\n    * **Thematic Specificity**: Do not just create a generic layout. Define a clear \"vibe\" or theme based on the content. Use specific aesthetic keywords (e.g., \"Glassmorphism\", \"Neobrutalism\", \"Minimalist\", \"Comic Book Style\") to guide the design.\n    * **Typography Hierarchy**: Explicitly import and use font pairings. Use a distinct Display Font for headers and a highly readable Body Font for text.\n    * **Readability**: Pay extra attention to readability. Ensure the text is always readable with sufficient contrast against the background. Choose fonts and colors that enhance legibility.\n\n**Design and Functionality:**\n    * **Component-Based Design**: Do not just dump text into blocks. Semanticize the content into distinct UI components.\n    * **Layout Dynamics**: Break the grid. Avoid strict, identical grid columns. Use asymmetrical layouts, Bento grids, or responsive flexbox layouts where some elements span full width to create visual interest and emphasize key content.\n    * **Tailwind Configuration**: Extend the Tailwind configuration within a `<script>` block to define custom font families and color palettes that match the theme.\n    * Thoroughly analyze the user's instructions to determine the desired type of webpage, application, or visualization. What are the key features, layouts, or functionality?\n    * Analyze any provided data to identify the most compelling layout or visualization of it. For example, if the user requests a visualization, select an appropriate chart type (bar, line, pie, scatter, etc.) to create the most insightful and visually compelling representation. Or if user instructions say `use a carousel format`, you should consider how to break the content and any media into different card components to display within the carousel.\n    * If requirements are underspecified, make reasonable assumptions to complete the design and functionality. Your goal is to deliver a working product with no placeholder content.\n    * Ensure the generated code is valid and functional. Return only the code, and open the HTML codeblock with the literal string \"```html\".\n    * The output must be a complete and valid HTML document with no placeholder content for the developer to fill in.\n\n**Libraries:**\n  Unless otherwise specified, use:\n    * Tailwind for CSS\n    * **CRITICAL: Use the Tailwind CDN from `https://cdn.tailwindcss.com`. Do NOT use `tailwind.min.css` or any other local Tailwind file. Always include Tailwind using: `<script src=\"https://cdn.tailwindcss.com\"></script>`**\n\n**Constraints:**\n  * **External Links:** You ARE allowed to generate external links (`<a href=\"...\">` and `window.open(...)`) to external websites (e.g. google.com, wikipedia.org) for user navigation.\n  * **NO External Embeds:** Do NOT embed any external resources (e.g. `<script src=\"...\">`, `<img src=\"...\">`, `<iframe src=\"...\">`, `<link href=\"...\">`) from external URLs. Content Security Policy (CSP) will block them.\n  * **Media Restriction:** ONLY use media URLs that are explicitly passed in the input. Do NOT generate or hallucinate any other media URLs (e.g. from placeholder sites or external CDNs).\n  * **Render All Media:** You MUST render ALL media (images, videos, audio) that are passed in. Do NOT skip or omit any provided media items. Every passed-in media URL must appear in the final HTML output.\n  * **Navigation Restriction:** Do NOT generate unneeded fake links or buttons to sub-pages (e.g. \"About\", \"Contact\", \"Learn More\") unless explicitly requested. Stick to the plan and the provided content.\n  * **Footer Restriction:** **NEVER** generate any footer content, including legal footers like \"All rights reserved\" or \"Copyright 2024\". [It is a violation of Google's policies to hallucinate legal footers.]\n"}],"role":"user"},"p-render-mode":"Auto","b-render-model-name":"gemini-flash"}},{"id":"ask_user_ai_system_specification","metadata":{"title":"Ai System Specification","visual":{"x":250,"y":300,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88}},"type":"embed://a2/a2.bgl.json#21ee02e7-83fa-49d0-964c-0cab10eafc2c","configuration":{"description":{"parts":[{"text":"Provide AI system architecture details"}],"role":"user"},"p-modality":"Any"}},{"id":"ask_user_firebase_project_id","metadata":{"title":"Firebase Project Id","visual":{"x":250,"y":450,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88}},"type":"embed://a2/a2.bgl.json#21ee02e7-83fa-49d0-964c-0cab10eafc2c","configuration":{"description":{"parts":[{"text":"Enter your Firebase project ID"}],"role":"user"},"p-modality":"Any"}},{"id":"ask_user_api_key","metadata":{"title":"Api Key","visual":{"x":250,"y":600,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88}},"type":"embed://a2/a2.bgl.json#21ee02e7-83fa-49d0-964c-0cab10eafc2c","configuration":{"description":{"parts":[{"text":"Provide your Firebase API key"}],"role":"user"},"p-modality":"Any"}},{"id":"ask_user_auth_domain","metadata":{"title":"Auth Domain","visual":{"x":250,"y":750,"collapsed":"expanded","outputHeight":88}},"type":"embed://a2/a2.bgl.json#21ee02e7-83fa-49d0-964c-0cab10eafc2c","configuration":{"description":{"parts":[{"text":"Specify your Firebase authentication domain"}],"role":"user"},"p-modality":"Any"}}],"edges":[{"from":"ask_user_ai_system_specification","to":"node_step_system_status_and_code_generation_report","out":"context","in":"p-z-ask_user_ai_system_specification"},{"from":"ask_user_api_key","to":"node_step_system_status_and_code_generation_report","out":"context","in":"p-z-ask_user_api_key"},{"from":"ask_user_auth_domain","to":"node_step_system_status_and_code_generation_report","out":"context","in":"p-z-ask_user_auth_domain"},{"from":"ask_user_firebase_project_id","to":"node_step_system_status_and_code_generation_report","out":"context","in":"p-z-ask_user_firebase_project_id"},{"from":"node_step_system_status_and_code_generation_report","to":"node_step_system_status_report","out":"context","in":"p-z-node_step_system_status_and_code_generation_report"}]}